It hides the truth.

01:01:55.600 --> 01:01:57.100
It throws away the evidence.

01:01:57.100 --> 01:02:02.120
It forces the caller higher up the chain to blindly guess what went wrong.

01:02:02.860 --> 01:02:10.580
A robust system should propagate the exact evidence of failure so that the caller can make a logically informed decision about how to actually recover.

01:02:10.580 --> 01:02:16.460
It's about preserving the absolute truth of the system at every single level of the stack.

01:02:17.040 --> 01:02:18.760
Don't swallow the error with a catch-all.

01:02:19.080 --> 01:02:21.220
Don't use mannequins for empty seats.

